WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.126
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.126 --> 00:00:05.251
<v Examiner>Define self-management of a long-term condition,

3
00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:08.962
<v Examiner>and describe the nurse's role in self-management support.

4
00:00:09.412 --> 00:00:14.727
Long-term conditions are ongoing or recurring conditions that significantly affect

5
00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:20.560
people's lives: diabetes, cancers, cardiovascular and respiratory disease, mental illness,

6
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.801
chronic pain, chronic kidney disease and dementia.

7
00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:28.208
They're rising in New Zealand, and many people have several at once,

8
00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:29.764
which is multimorbidity.

9
00:00:30.214 --> 00:00:35.630
Self-management is any way a person with a long-term condition manages it themselves.

10
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.115
It's an ongoing process, not a one-off.

11
00:00:38.115 --> 00:00:43.212
People with these conditions spend only a few hours a year with health services;

12
00:00:43.212 --> 00:00:45.952
the rest of the time they're self-managing.

13
00:00:45.952 --> 00:00:48.628
A good self-manager knows their condition,

14
00:00:48.628 --> 00:00:53.407
follows a plan agreed with their health professionals, shares in decisions,

15
00:00:53.407 --> 00:00:56.975
monitors their symptoms, and adopts a healthy lifestyle.

16
00:00:57.425 --> 00:01:01.940
Self-management support is the help given so they can manage day to day,

17
00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.885
as a collaborative partnership.

18
00:01:03.885 --> 00:01:06.331
The nurse's role, from Janine's slides.

19
00:01:06.331 --> 00:01:11.536
Give information that helps people make informed decisions and set their own goals.

20
00:01:11.536 --> 00:01:13.919
Encourage them to take an active part,

21
00:01:13.919 --> 00:01:17.369
acknowledging that they are experts in their own lives.

22
00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:22.762
Support them to join self-management groups, and advocate for groups where none exist.

23
00:01:22.762 --> 00:01:25.146
Make sure it's culturally appropriate.

24
00:01:25.146 --> 00:01:28.846
Follow up after education programmes, with regular updates.

25
00:01:28.846 --> 00:01:31.480
And refer to support agencies when needed.

26
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.553
The quiz word for the nurse's role is empowering.

27
00:01:35.003 --> 00:01:39.486
Good programmes have four components: health literacy, cultural relevance,

28
00:01:39.486 --> 00:01:44.514
behaviour change, and the health professional's role in supporting self-management.

29
00:01:44.514 --> 00:01:49.663
Equity matters here too: care shouldn't vary in quality because of gender, ethnicity,

30
00:01:49.663 --> 00:01:51.238
where you live, or income.

31
00:01:51.688 --> 00:01:57.206
Long-term conditions: ongoing or recurring, often several at once, multimorbidity.

32
00:01:57.206 --> 00:02:01.916
Self-management: the person manages it themselves, every day, ongoing.

33
00:02:01.916 --> 00:02:05.886
Nurse's role: information for informed decisions and goals,

34
00:02:05.886 --> 00:02:11.538
treat them as experts in their own lives, groups, cultural fit, follow-up, referral.

35
00:02:11.538 --> 00:02:13.085
The word is empowering.
